                  "name": "State mapping heading",
                  "fill": "$ink",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Keep the state vocabulary honest",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "TUya9",
                  "name": "SDK state mapping",
                  "fill": "$ink-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "input-streaming → Preparing input\ninput-available → Running\noutput-available → Completed\noutput-error → Could not complete\napproval-requested → Needs approval\napproval-responded → Approved or declined, not “saved”\noutput-denied → Declined\n\nStopped and outcome unknown are Tabra recovery states. Render a separate notice; do not invent SDK enum values. A write is successful only after its result or receipt is confirmed.\n\nPending phases show a separate status hint, never fabricated tool output. Inspect approval.approved rather than assuming every approval response means yes. Tabra intentionally leaves successful tools collapsed, even though the library example opens them.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
